From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: steamac <steamac@local>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 01:30:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 44/44] kk: run unroll kernels before the render pass instead
 of ending it

STEAMAC-G. Indexed draws that need an unroll (a flat varying with the last
vertex provoking, which zink keeps; fans, 8-bit indices, restart) ran the
unroll kernel in a compute pass that ended the render pass around every such
draw: attachments stored, the compute pass, attachments loaded again. 0041
writes the indices of direct non-indexed draws on the CPU; those of indexed
draws are in memory the GPU may write before the render pass (a copy earlier
in the command buffer, submissions still running), so the CPU can read them
neither at recording nor at submission. With 0041 a traced Steam boot still
had 194 web helper command buffers with unroll kernels, the longest 13.8 ms
of GPU time on an M1 Max with 37 render passes (4 at 4x MSAA).

Vulkan does not allow writing index, indirect or predicate data inside a
render pass (no transfers there, and a self-dependency cannot order shader
writes before index or indirect reads), so these kernels can run before it.
Dispatches recorded with pre_gfx (kk_dispatch_precomp's parameter, unused so
far; hk's meaning) while a render encoder is open go into a compute pass in a
Metal command buffer of its own, committed right before the render encoder's:
a render encoder starts a Metal command buffer when the one being encoded
already has an encoder, and a command buffer commits all of its Metal command
buffers in order. pre_gfx are the predicates of draws and the unrolls of draws
without a geometry shader (geometry and adjacency); tessellation, geometry
shaders and the unrolls a passthrough GS reads still end the render encoder.
The geometry heap is reset for the render encoder whose draws use it and freed
when that one ends, no longer at every render encoder start (an unroll before
a render encoder and a GS compute pass ending it keep apart).

host/moltenvk/repro provoking_last.c: 11 indexed draws whose indices a
vkCmdUpdateBuffer earlier in the command buffer writes: 12 render passes and
12 compute passes, 2.2 ms of GPU time -> 1 render pass and 2 compute passes
(the update, the unrolls), 0.33 ms; indexed indirect draws with a geometry
shader draw among them: 12 render passes, 2.24 ms -> 2, 0.59 ms.
